# lucid-data-v1 -- the first-run bundle: the files a fresh clone needs beside the tracked config/
# and data/<material>/<particle>/<kind>/emitter.json. Published as a GitHub release asset (release
# tag = this tag); scripts/download_data.py installs it into data/ and checks every file against
# the tracked data/MANIFEST.sha256.
#
# The weights, the event slices and the overlap tables are on no ref, so they are staged under
# $LUCID_ASSET_SRC (a directory laid out like data/, plus spatial_overlap_integrals/): the four
# weights.npz copied in, the tables built cold with
#
#   python tools/build_overlap_tables.py <repo> "$LUCID_ASSET_SRC"
#
# and each slice cut with
#
#   python tools/slice_root.py <source ROOT> "$LUCID_ASSET_SRC"/water/<dir>/<name>.root --events <N>
#
# from the source each `origin:` line names. Then
#
#   LUCID_ASSET_OUT=<dir> tools/make_asset.sh tools/assets/lucid-data-v1.manifest
#
# Publishing (by hand, owner): copy the data rows of <dir>/lucid-data-v1.MANIFEST.sha256 (every row
# but INDEX.md and PROVENANCE.txt, without the leading ./) into data/MANIFEST.sha256 and commit it,
# then `gh release create lucid-data-v1 <dir>/lucid-data-v1.tar.gz`. A re-cut slice has new bytes
# (ROOT stamps a UUID and dates), so a rebuild re-copies the rows. A new version is a new tag: one
# commit changes RELEASE in scripts/download_data.py and data/MANIFEST.sha256 together.
