# lucid-data-v1

**The files a fresh LUCiD clone needs beside the tracked configuration**: the weights of the four
SIREN emitters LUCiD ships, five real GEANT4 (PhotonSim) events of a 1 GeV muon, six of a 1.5 GeV
muon, and the overlap tables the shipped code loads. Install it from the repository root with

    python scripts/download_data.py

which fetches this tarball from the `lucid-data-v1` GitHub release (or, with `--from-dir DIR`,
from a local copy), checks every file against the repository's `data/MANIFEST.sha256` and only
then moves the files into `data/` (the overlap tables into `spatial_overlap_integrals/` at the
repository root).

## What is in this tarball

| path | what it is |
|---|---|
| `water/muon/cherenkov/weights.npz` | Cherenkov µ emitter (seed 1 of the `water_mu_seed_scan_p100_ti02_n150k` scan) |
| `water/muon/dedx/weights.npz` | dE/dx µ emitter (seed 9 of `water_mu_dedx_seed_scan_nominal`) |
| `water/electron/cherenkov/weights.npz` | Cherenkov e emitter (seed 5 of `water_el_seed_scan_p100_ti02_n150k`) |
| `water/electron/dedx/weights.npz` | dE/dx e emitter (seed 7 of `water_el_dedx_seed_scan_p100_ti02_n150k`) |
| `water/muon/1000MeV_5events.root` | events 0-4 of a 1 GeV muon PhotonSim file, every branch verbatim |
| `water/muon/1500MeV_6events.root` | events 0-5 of a 1.5 GeV muon PhotonSim file (the paper's cylinder display, event 5) |
| `spatial_overlap_integrals/*.json` | the 12 sensor-overlap tables (below) |
| `MANIFEST.sha256`, `PROVENANCE.txt` | sha256 of every file; the build's commit and sources |

Each weights file is a 3×256 SIREN in float32 (797 626 bytes, flat keys
`params_<layer>_Dense_0_<kernel|bias>`, read by `lucid.siren.emitter.read_weights`; no pickle).
Everything else an emitter needs (network shape, input domain, decoder, the s_max / N_photons /
t0 fits, provenance and training recipe) is the `emitter.json` tracked beside it. wbls and ice run
these water emitters (`config/materials/<material>.json`, key `"siren"`).

## The event slices

`tools/slice_root.py` cut each from the file its `origin:` line in `PROVENANCE.txt` names, with
ROOT's `TTree::CopyTree`, which copies every branch verbatim: the leading `OpticalPhotons` entries
(one entry per event), the leading `OpticalPhotonsRaw` photon chunks, those of the same events (3 per
event), and every histogram whole. Every `lucid.sources.root_reader` entry point returns
byte-identical arrays for each slice's events from the slice and from its source. They cover the
paper's display figures (`fig_charge_displays` entry 3 and `fig_juno_wbls` entry 0 of the 1 GeV
slice, `fig_cylinder_2d_displays` entry 5 of the 1.5 GeV slice, `fig_photon_event_display` event 0),
`examples/seed_reconstruct.py --geant4`, `examples/hello_multiparticle.py` (events 0 and 1 of the
1 GeV slice, one rotated) and the data tests.

uproot cannot cut these slices: it cannot write a `std::vector<std::string>` branch, and
`TrackInfo_CreatorProcess`, which `lucid/sources/root_reader.py` reads, is one.

## The overlap tables

`lucid.overlap.create_overlap_prob(sigma, r)` integrates a Gaussian photon spot of width
`sigma = temperature × sensor radius` over a disc sensor of radius `r` and caches the result as
`gaussian_overlap_r{r:.6f}_sigma{sigma:.6f}_ksig8_nd400_f64.json`. Every table the shipped code
asks for is here, so no first run waits for one (each takes one to two minutes on one core):

| r (m) | σ (m) | temperature | loaded by |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0.040 | 0.0080 | 0.2 | WCTE_like, WCTE, the tests' tiny geometry |
| 0.050 | 0.0100 | 0.2 | TAO |
| 0.075 | 0.0150 | 0.2 | IWCD, MidBox |
| 0.080 | 0.0160 | 0.2 | nuSCOPE |
| 0.100 | 0.0200 | 0.2 | EOS |
| 0.165 | 0.0330 | 0.2 | IceCube86 (`hello_telescope.py`) |
| 0.250 | 0.0500 | 0.2 | SK_like, SK_like_wbls, JUNO, JUNO_wbls (`hello_simulate.py`, `hello_gradient.py`) |
| 0.254 | 0.0508 | 0.2 | SK, HK, SK_WAND, HK_WAND |
| 0.500 | 0.1000 | 0.2 | BigHK |
| 0.250 | 0.0250 | 0.1 | `lucid.fitting.recon.MODEL_RECIPE` on SK_like: the paper's reconstruction, `seed_reconstruct.py` |
| 0.250 | 0.0125 | 0.05 | `fig_charge_displays.py` (SK_like, JUNO), `fig_cylinder_2d_displays.py` |
| 0.110 | 0.0055 | 0.05 | `fig_charge_displays.py`'s box |

Production (`lucid-run-job`, temperature 0) and `temperature=None` use no table. A table is
reproducible bit for bit on one CPU type; built on another, up to a few hundred float32 ulps
(≤ 1e-6) of its values can differ (XLA's CPU code). Each was built through
`DetectorGeometry.from_config`, the simulator's own path, so its name and bytes are what a cold
first use on that node writes.

Not in this bundle: the 500-event files the paper's tracking scans read (not distributed;
`analysis/paper/utils/generate_data.py` regenerates them on S3DF). The scans' results, which the
figures draw, are the `lucid-paper-results-v1` asset (`python scripts/download_data.py --paper`).
